     {"question": "How do I schedule a post for future publication?", "answer": "Set the publishedAt date to a future date and status to published. The post will appear once that date passes. Note: this requires ISR or rebuild to take effect."},
     {"question": "Can I use MDX instead of Markdoc?", "answer": "Makerkit uses Markdoc by default through Keystatic. You can create a custom CMS client for MDX, but you'll need to handle rendering differently."},
     {"question": "How do I add custom components to posts?", "answer": "Define custom Markdoc tags in your Keystatic configuration. Components like alerts, callouts, and code blocks are already available."},
     {"question": "Where are images stored?", "answer": "Store images in the public/images/blog/ directory and reference them with absolute paths like /images/blog/my-image.webp."},
     {"question": "How do I enable RSS feeds?", "answer": "RSS is generated automatically at /blog/rss.xml. The feed includes all published posts sorted by date."},
